 "intro": "At Lautulae, a narrow pass near Tarracina on the road from Rome to Campania, 315 BC. You are the dictator Quintus Fabius Maximus Rullianus, facing a Samnite army that has come down to the coast. The sources say little about this battle.",
 "debrief": "Little is known. Livy reports that the Romans were defeated at Lautulae; he notes that some writers said the battle was drawn, but that the master of horse, Quintus Aulius Cerretanus, died charging the enemy after killing the Samnite cavalry commander. The defeat shook Rome’s hold on Campania for a time, but Rome recovered and won again the next year. Most details here are reconstructions; the other choices are what-ifs.",
